    :root {
      --paper: #fcfbf7;
      --ink: #14171a;
      --accent: #173a55;
      --muted: #4d565d;
      --rule: #9da8af;
      --soft: #eef1f2;
      --soft-2: #f5f6f4;
    }

    @page { size: Letter; margin: 0; }
    * { box-sizing: border-box; }
    html, body {
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      background: var(--paper);
      color: var(--ink);
    }
    body {
      font-family: "Atkinson Next", Arial, sans-serif;
      font-size: 10.5pt;
      line-height: 1.4;
      -webkit-print-color-adjust: exact;
      print-color-adjust: exact;
    }
    .page {
      position: relative;
      width: 8.5in;
      height: 11in;
      overflow: hidden;
      padding: .58in .64in .55in;
      background: var(--paper);
      break-after: page;
      page-break-after: always;
    }
    .page:last-child { break-after: auto; page-break-after: auto; }
    .top-rule {
      position: absolute;
      top: 0;
      left: .64in;
      right: .64in;
      height: .10in;
      background: var(--accent);
    }
    .eyebrow {
      margin: .10in 0 .18in;
      color: var(--accent);
      font-family: "Atkinson Mono", monospace;
      font-size: 8.2pt;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: .08em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }
    h1, h2, h3, p { margin-top: 0; }
    h1 {
      max-width: 6.95in;
      margin-bottom: .17in;
      font-size: 28pt;
      line-height: 1.01;
      letter-spacing: -.025em;
      font-weight: 700;
    }
    h2 {
      margin-bottom: .14in;
      font-size: 20pt;
      line-height: 1.08;
      letter-spacing: -.018em;
    }
    h3 {
      margin-bottom: .07in;
      color: var(--accent);
      font-family: "Atkinson Mono", monospace;
      font-size: 8.2pt;
      line-height: 1.2;
      letter-spacing: .055em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }
    .deck {
      max-width: 6.4in;
      margin-bottom: .20in;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 11.5pt;
      line-height: 1.35;
    }
    .status-row {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: .12in;
      margin-bottom: .22in;
    }
    .status {
      display: inline-block;
      padding: .055in .11in .045in;
      border: 1px solid var(--accent);
      background: var(--accent);
      color: var(--paper);
      font-family: "Atkinson Mono", monospace;
      font-size: 8.1pt;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: .06em;
    }
    .status-note {
      color: var(--muted);
      font-family: "Atkinson Mono", monospace;
      font-size: 8.4pt;
    }
    .hero {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1.28fr 1fr;
      gap: .16in;
      margin-bottom: .15in;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
      padding: .17in 0 .15in;
    }
    .hero-number {
      font-family: "Atkinson Mono", monospace;
      font-size: 43pt;
      font-weight: 700;
      line-height: .93;
      letter-spacing: -.045em;
    }
    .hero-unit {
      margin-top: .04in;
      color: var(--accent);
      font-size: 13pt;
      font-weight: 700;
    }
    .hero-size {
      align-self: end;
      color: var(--muted);
      text-align: right;
    }
    .hero-size strong {
      display: block;
      color: var(--ink);
      font-family: "Atkinson Mono", monospace;
      font-size: 13.2pt;
      line-height: 1.15;
    }
    .hero-size span {
      display: block;
      margin-top: .08in;
    }
    .finding {
      margin: 0 0 .17in;
      padding: .13in .16in;
      border-left: .07in solid var(--accent);
      background: var(--soft);
      font-size: 10.8pt;
      line-height: 1.36;
    }
    .finding strong { color: var(--accent); }
    .metrics {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
      gap: .12in;
      margin-bottom: .17in;
    }
    .metric {
      min-height: .76in;
      padding: .11in .13in;
      background: var(--soft-2);
      border-top: 2px solid var(--accent);
    }
    .metric strong {
      display: block;
      font-family: "Atkinson Mono", monospace;
      font-size: 19pt;
      line-height: 1;
    }
    .metric span {
      display: block;
      margin-top: .05in;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 8.7pt;
    }
    .destination {
      padding: .13in .16in;
      border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    }
    .destination-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: .85in 1fr;
      gap: .045in .12in;
      margin: 0;
    }
    .destination-grid dt {
      color: var(--muted);
      font-family: "Atkinson Mono", monospace;
      font-size: 8.2pt;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }
    .destination-grid dd {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: "Atkinson Mono", monospace;
      font-size: 8.6pt;
      overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    }
    .section-lead {
      max-width: 6.55in;
      margin-bottom: .15in;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 10.7pt;
    }
    table {
      width: 100%;
      border-collapse: collapse;
      margin: 0 0 .14in;
      font-size: 8.5pt;
      line-height: 1.2;
    }
    caption {
      margin-bottom: .07in;
      color: var(--muted);
      text-align: left;
      font-size: 8.5pt;
    }
    thead { display: table-header-group; }
    thead th {
      padding: .055in .065in;
      border-top: 2px solid var(--accent);
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
      color: var(--accent);
      font-family: "Atkinson Mono", monospace;
      font-size: 7.6pt;
      letter-spacing: .045em;
      text-align: left;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }
    tbody th, tbody td {
      padding: .052in .065in;
      border-bottom: 1px solid #d7dcde;
      vertical-align: top;
      text-align: left;
    }
    tbody th { font-weight: 600; }
    td.count, td.bytes {
      white-space: nowrap;
      font-family: "Atkinson Mono", monospace;
      text-align: right;
    }
    tfoot th, tfoot td {
      padding: .065in;
      border-top: 2px solid var(--accent);
      font-weight: 700;
    }
    tfoot td {
      font-family: "Atkinson Mono", monospace;
      text-align: right;
    }
    code, .mono { font-family: "Atkinson Mono", monospace; font-size: .94em; }
    a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: underline; }
    .two-col {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: .15in;
    }
    .card {
      padding: .12in .15in;
      background: var(--soft-2);
      border-top: 2px solid var(--accent);
    }
    .card p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
    .card ul { margin: .05in 0 0 .16in; padding: 0; }
    .card li { margin-bottom: .035in; }
    .label {
      display: inline-block;
      margin-right: .05in;
      color: var(--accent);
      font-family: "Atkinson Mono", monospace;
      font-size: 7.6pt;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: .045em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }
    .steps {
      margin: .01in 0 .13in;
      padding: 0;
      list-style: none;
      counter-reset: step;
      font-size: 9.8pt;
    }
    .steps li {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: .37in 1fr;
      gap: .10in;
      padding: .055in 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid #d7dcde;
      counter-increment: step;
    }
    .steps li::before {
      content: "0" counter(step);
      color: var(--accent);
      font-family: "Atkinson Mono", monospace;
      font-size: 9pt;
      font-weight: 700;
    }
    .boundary {
      margin: .09in 0 .12in;
      padding: .11in .14in;
      border: 1px solid var(--accent);
      background: var(--soft);
      font-size: 9.4pt;
    }
    .boundary p { margin-bottom: .05in; }
    .boundary p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
    .evidence {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: .075in .16in;
      margin-top: .05in;
      font-size: 8.3pt;
    }
    .evidence div {
      padding-top: .055in;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    }
    .evidence strong {
      display: block;
      color: var(--accent);
      font-family: "Atkinson Mono", monospace;
      font-size: 7.5pt;
      letter-spacing: .04em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }
    .digest { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
    .footer {
      position: absolute;
      left: .64in;
      right: .64in;
      bottom: .24in;
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
      padding-top: .07in;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
      color: var(--muted);
      font-family: "Atkinson Mono", monospace;
      font-size: 7.5pt;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main>
    <section class="page" aria-labelledby="report-title">
      <div class="top-rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Cartofreako · active archive check-in · release v12</p>
      <h1 id="report-title">cartofreako v12 checked in to UCB Active Archive Object Storage</h1>
      <p class="deck">An evidence-first record of the generated-assets v12 release deposited at its immutable public prefix.</p>

      <div class="status-row">
        <span class="status">OBSERVED · VERIFIED</span>
        <span class="status-note">@@VERIFIED_AT@@ · run @@RUN_ID@@</span>
      </div>

      <div class="hero" aria-label="Final remote inventory, stored size, and extracted package payload">
        <div>
          <div class="hero-number">594</div>
          <div class="hero-unit">objects in the completed release</div>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-size">
          <strong>2,039,067,910 bytes</strong>
          1.90 GiB stored at the verified prefix
          <span><strong>2,322,788,028 bytes</strong>2.16 GiB extracted package payload</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="finding"><strong>Observed result.</strong> The local 594-object release and remote prefix agreed after <code>release.json</code> was published last. @@DOWNLOAD_SENTENCE@@</p>

      <div class="metrics" aria-label="Release summary metrics">
        <div class="metric"><strong>187</strong><span>explicit SVG-gzip objects</span></div>
        <div class="metric"><strong>187</strong><span>single-page PDF maps</span></div>
        <div class="metric"><strong>215</strong><span>full and thumbnail PNG files</span></div>
      </div>

      <section class="destination" aria-labelledby="destination-heading">
        <h3 id="destination-heading">Archive destination</h3>
        <dl class="destination-grid">
          <dt>Endpoint</dt><dd>https://s3-ewh.ist.berkeley.edu</dd>
          <dt>Region</dt><dd>us-east-1</dd>
          <dt>Bucket</dt><dd>adekosnik-bucket01</dd>
          <dt>Prefix</dt><dd>cartofreako/v12/</dd>
        </dl>
      </section>

      <div class="footer"><span>Cartofreako / v12 / UCB Active Archive</span><span>1 / 3</span></div>
    </section>

    <section class="page" aria-labelledby="inventory-title">
      <div class="top-rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Deposit inventory</p>
      <h2 id="inventory-title">What was uploaded</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">Counts and stored-byte totals below are exact for the completed prefix. The recovery package remains byte-for-byte identical to the GitHub release asset.</p>

      <table aria-label="Uploaded Cartofreako v12 object families">
        <caption>Completed object families beneath <code>cartofreako/v12/</code>.</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Object family</th><th scope="col">Purpose</th><th scope="col">Count</th><th scope="col">Bytes</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row"><code>tree/svg/*.svg.gz</code></th><td>Explicit browser-decompressed SVG archives</td><td class="count">187</td><td class="bytes">353,763,415</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row"><code>tree/pdf/*.pdf</code></th><td>Single-page print maps</td><td class="count">187</td><td class="bytes">567,476,883</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row"><code>tree/png/*.png</code></th><td>Full-size opaque PNG maps</td><td class="count">187</td><td class="bytes">188,872,394</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row"><code>tree/thumbnail/cahill-keyes/*.png</code></th><td>480 × 240 contact-sheet previews</td><td class="count">28</td><td class="bytes">1,129,282</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row"><code>package/assets.generated.v12.tar.xz</code></th><td>Byte-identical recovery package</td><td class="count">1</td><td class="bytes">927,742,112</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row"><code>README.md</code></th><td>Release layout and delivery contract</td><td class="count">1</td><td class="bytes">2,099</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row"><code>viewer.html</code></th><td>Same-origin streaming SVG viewer</td><td class="count">1</td><td class="bytes">3,469</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row"><code>SHA256SUMS</code></th><td>SHA-256 payload manifest</td><td class="count">1</td><td class="bytes">76,066</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row"><code>release.json</code></th><td>Release record and completion marker</td><td class="count">1</td><td class="bytes">2,190</td></tr>
        </tbody>
        <tfoot>
          <tr><th scope="row" colspan="2">Completed release</th><td>594</td><td>2,039,067,910</td></tr>
        </tfoot>
      </table>

      <div class="two-col">
        <section class="card" aria-labelledby="browser-use-title">
          <h3 id="browser-use-title">Browser delivery</h3>
          <p><span class="label">Observed</span>The documentation grid embeds 28 PNG previews. Each selection opens the same-origin viewer, which streams one <code>.svg.gz</code> response through <code>DecompressionStream("gzip")</code>. SVG gzip responses use <code>application/gzip</code> without <code>Content-Encoding</code>.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="card" aria-labelledby="package-title">
          <h3 id="package-title">Recovery identity</h3>
          <p><span class="label">Observed</span>The 927,742,112-byte XZ package has SHA-256 <span class="mono digest">dc1d761def31d77a05a7cc42f9bc0705ee864046f2e235f50c701c9c42fe960a</span>.</p>
        </section>
      </div>

      <div class="boundary">
        <p><span class="label">Observed</span>The delivery tree contains no raw SVG, symlink, zero-byte file, or temporary upload artifact. The unchanged recovery package retains its original 673-file <code>assets.generated/</code> tree.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="footer"><span>Cartofreako / deposit inventory</span><span>2 / 3</span></div>
    </section>

    <section class="page" aria-labelledby="verification-title">
      <div class="top-rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Verification and evidence boundary</p>
      <h2 id="verification-title">How the check-in was verified</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">The uploader used an ephemeral rclone configuration, credentials entered on <code>/dev/tty</code>, and two exact typed confirmations before changing the incomplete prefix.</p>

      <ol class="steps">
        <li><span><strong>Local preflight.</strong> Archive identity, the 592-entry payload manifest, SHA-256 hashes, JSON syntax, gzip integrity, fixed inventories, and release hygiene passed.</span></li>
        <li><span><strong>Destination gate.</strong> The exact bucket and prefix were readable. Inventory found only two known objects from an incomplete attempt and no completion marker.</span></li>
        <li><span><strong>Intentional cleanup.</strong> After a second exact-object confirmation, uploader 4 removed only obsolete key <code>tree/svg/geometry-ck-44-22.svg</code>. The retained PNG pilot received its missing cache metadata.</span></li>
        <li><span><strong>Browser pilots.</strong> Public SVG-gzip and PNG stored bytes and HTTP metadata passed; the same-origin viewer was retrieved and checked before bulk completion.</span></li>
        <li><span><strong>Immutable copy.</strong> General and SVG-gzip phases used <code>rclone copy --checksum --immutable --check-first</code>. No <code>sync</code> or <code>move</code> operation was used.</span></li>
        <li><span><strong>Completion ordering.</strong> The 592 payload objects passed <code>rclone check --one-way</code>; <code>release.json</code> was then uploaded as object 594 and the complete release was checked again.</span></li>
        <li><span><strong>Full read-back.</strong> @@DOWNLOAD_STEP@@ Remote count and bytes matched local state: 594 objects and 2,039,067,910 bytes.</span></li>
      </ol>

      <section class="boundary" aria-labelledby="boundary-title">
        <h3 id="boundary-title">Evidence boundary</h3>
        <p><span class="label">Observed</span>After upload, anonymous HTTPS returned the exact local marker and viewer, all 28 grid previews and 28 linked SVG-gzip objects responded, pilot bytes and metadata matched, and Chrome rendered a live decompressed SVG.</p>
        <p><span class="label">@@DOWNLOAD_LABEL@@</span>@@DOWNLOAD_BOUNDARY@@</p>
        <p><span class="label">Unavailable</span>Peak uploader RSS and the network route used by the operator were not independently recorded; neither is inferred from byte totals.</p>
      </section>

      <div class="two-col">
        <section class="card" aria-labelledby="source-title">
          <h3 id="source-title">Source identity</h3>
          <p>Git tag <code>v20260807</code> resolves to source commit <code>2bd3d760fef540addfcbb4f8002ef7b283d8000f</code>. The source and generated recovery package remain separate release assets.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="card" aria-labelledby="marker-title">
          <h3 id="marker-title">Completion semantics</h3>
          <p><a href="https://s3-ewh.ist.berkeley.edu/adekosnik-bucket01/cartofreako/v12/release.json">The public release marker</a> has <code>complete: true</code> and was published last. Post-publication reports remain outside the immutable prefix.</p>
        </section>
      </div>

      <h3 style="margin-top:.12in">Evidence register</h3>
      <div class="evidence">
        <div><strong>Manifest</strong><span class="mono">SHA256SUMS</span> · 592 payload entries</div>
        <div><strong>Manifest SHA-256</strong><span class="mono digest">88302648b9bed3775d708cc1d0e959c6973f01ede09ae9a5c5a4bb4f7c12ce38</span></div>
        <div><strong>Release marker</strong><span class="mono">release.json</span> · 594-object completion record</div>
        <div><strong>Uploader</strong><span class="mono">upload-generated-assets-s3-release.sh</span> · version 4 · run @@RUN_ID@@</div>
      </div>

      <div class="footer"><span>Cartofreako / verified archive record / @@VERIFIED_AT@@</span><span>3 / 3</span></div>
    </section>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
